-- title:
--   Integral weight-k forms on Γ₁(M) with independent reductions
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\kappa$ a field of characteristic $p$; let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $k$ be a natural number with $3 \le k$. Then there exist a natural number $d$, a family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to M_k(\Gamma_1(M))$ of modular forms of weight $k$ (as an integer) for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M)$, and a family $pg : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ of integral power series such that: (i) for each $i$, the image of $pg\,i$ under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the $q$-expansion of $g\,i$ of width $1$, i.e. `IsIntegralQExp (g i) (pg i)` holds; (ii) the Laurent series over $\kappa$ obtained from $pg\,i$ by reducing coefficients along $\mathbb{Z} \to \kappa$ and regarding the resulting power series as a Laurent series, namely `intSeriesC κ (pg i)`, form a $\kappa$-linearly independent family indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$; and (iii) the numerical bound
--   $$(k-1)\,[\,\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(M)\sqcup\langle -1\rangle\,] + 6\,\#\bigl(\Gamma_1(M)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) / \langle T, -1\rangle\bigr) \le 12 d$$
--   holds, where the first term uses the index of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ and $-1$, and the second the cardinality of the double coset space of $\Gamma_1(M)$ and the subgroup generated by $T$ and $-1$.
--
--   The bound on $d$ is the classical dimension formula for $M_k(\Gamma_1(M))$ with $k \ge 3$, $M \ge 5$ (no elliptic points, all cusps regular), rewritten via $12(g-1) = [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_1(M)] - 6c$ so that only group-theoretic quantities appear; the assertion supplies a large supply of weight-$k$ forms with integral $q$-expansions whose reductions stay independent over $\kappa$. It is used in the study of orders of vanishing on the function field of $X_1(M)$, in [`ModularCurve.exists_ord_eq_zero_of_ord_pos_x1FunctionFieldC`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_ord_eq_zero_of_ord_pos_x1FunctionFieldC), [`ModularCurve.twelve_dvd_ord_of_coe_eq_div_of_ord_nonneg_x1FunctionFieldC`](thm.html#ModularCurve.twelve_dvd_ord_of_coe_eq_div_of_ord_nonneg_x1FunctionFieldC) and [`ModularCurve.twelve_dvd_ord_sub_ord_of_coe_eq_div_of_ord_neg_x1FunctionFieldC`](thm.html#ModularCurve.twelve_dvd_ord_sub_ord_of_coe_eq_div_of_ord_neg_x1FunctionFieldC).
